@startuml 03-server-data-model
title Architecture 03 - Server data model (portable SQL: SQLite and Postgres)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
hide circle
hide methods

entity "accounts" as accounts {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * next_seq : integer
  * gc_floor : integer
  * recovery_verifier_hash : blob
  * created_at : timestamp
}

entity "account_identities" as identities {
  * provider : text <<PK>>
  * subject : text <<PK>>
  --
  * account_id : uuid <<FK, unique>>
}

entity "pairing_approvals" as approvals {
  * pairing_id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * pake_msg_existing : blob
  * wrapped_nonce : blob
  * wrapped_ciphertext : blob
}

entity "oidc_nonces" as nonces {
  * nonce_hash : blob <<PK>>
  --
  * provider : text
  * expires_at : timestamp
}

entity "devices" as devices {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * account_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * name : text
  * token_hash : blob <<unique>>
  * last_cursor : integer
  * last_seen_at : timestamp
  * created_at : timestamp
  * revoked_at : timestamp (0 = active)
}

entity "blocks" as blocks {
  * account_id : uuid <<PK, FK>>
  * block_id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * note_id : uuid
  * version : text
  * deleted : boolean
  * nonce : blob
  * ciphertext : blob
  * seq : integer
  * origin_device_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * received_at : timestamp
}

entity "blobs" as blobs {
  * account_id : uuid <<PK, FK>>
  * hash : blob <<PK>>
  --
  * size : integer
  * created_at : timestamp
}

entity "pairings" as pairings {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * channel : text <<unique>>
  * poll_token_hash : blob
  * device_name : text
  * pake_msg_new : blob
  * state : text
  * account_id : text ('' until claimed)
  * expires_at : timestamp
}

accounts ||--o{ devices
accounts ||--o{ blocks
accounts ||--o{ blobs
accounts |o--o{ pairings
accounts ||--o| identities
pairings ||--o| approvals
devices ||--o{ blocks

note right of blocks
  One row per block: only the newest version is kept.
  Index (account_id, seq) serves the change feed.
  version is a fixed-width hybrid logical clock string,
  compared bytewise.
  A deleted block is a tombstone with empty ciphertext.
end note

note right of accounts
  next_seq is incremented in the same transaction
  that stores a block, so seq is gap-free and
  strictly increasing per account.
end note

note bottom of pairings
  state: pending -> claimed -> approved, then deleted on delivery.
  Rows expire after 5 minutes and are removed by GcJob.
  A pairing can be claimed once, and only the claiming account can approve.
  The device and its token are created at delivery, so no token is
  ever stored in clear text.
end note

note bottom of identities
  Binds an account to one OIDC identity (issuer id + subject).
  One identity owns at most one account.
end note

note bottom of nonces
  Nonces for OIDC logins: issued by the server, valid 10 minutes,
  deleted on first use. Only the hash is stored.
end note

legend right
  Logical type mapping
  | Logical | SQLite | Postgres |
  | uuid | TEXT, canonical form | TEXT, canonical form |
  | blob | BLOB | BYTEA |
  | text | TEXT | TEXT |
  | integer | INTEGER | BIGINT |
  | boolean | INTEGER 0 or 1 | BIGINT 0 or 1 |
  | timestamp | INTEGER, unix ms | BIGINT, unix ms |

  Portability rules (as implemented)
  1. Only text, 64-bit integers and blobs are used, and no column is ever NULL.
  2. Timestamps are unix milliseconds, set by the server, never by the database.
  3. Ids and seq are generated by the server, no auto-increment or sequences.
  4. version is compared in the server, not by the database, so collation is irrelevant.
  5. Upserts use INSERT ... ON CONFLICT ... DO UPDATE, which both support.
  6. No triggers, stored procedures or database-specific functions.
  7. Every write transaction starts by updating the account row. That takes the
     write lock in SQLite and the row lock in Postgres, so pushes are serialised
     per account and the change feed never shows a higher seq before a lower one.
end legend

note bottom of devices
  last_cursor is updated on every pull.
  GcJob removes tombstones below the lowest
  last_cursor of all active devices.
end note

@enduml
